Are stiletto french tips hard to maintain? Not especially, though the point itself is the most delicate part of any stiletto nail regardless of the tip design, so gentle handling around edges and corners matters more here than length maintenance does. A gel or hard gel topcoat helps protect the fine detail work at the tip specifically. Builder gel apex placement, meaning where the nail's structural high point sits, also affects how the smile line appears to sit on the nail once it is cured, which is why salon-applied gel-X or acrylic extensions tend to produce a cleaner result than natural nail application alone.

The most common mistake on a first attempt is placing the guide too straight across, which flattens the V and makes it look like a slightly crooked classic French rather than an intentional V-cut. Following the nail's own angle, rather than a straight horizontal line, is the fix.

