## Finding Your Stiletto French Tip Look

None of these five categories is the "right" version of a stiletto French. That is the actual point. The V-cut earns its place as the 2026 baseline because the geometry genuinely fits the shape, not because it is the only option worth wearing. Chrome and black push the same structure toward something bolder. Pastel softens it. Micro strips it down to a single confident line.

What matters now is being able to name the one that is yours, specifically, rather than screenshotting another ten photos and hoping a nail tech guesses correctly. Bring the finish, the depth of the V, and the base color into that conversation, and the appointment goes faster and the result matches what you actually pictured. Stiletto was never a shape that asked to be safe. The French tip, done right, does not ask it to be either.
